 ## Host-Side MSBuild Tests (full-build — requires local SDK)
 
+The experimental Kotlin device/package probes additionally require the local
+SDK, a built `src/Microsoft.Android.Kotlin/Microsoft.Android.Kotlin.csproj`,
+and an Android device. See `external/Java.Interop/tests/generator-Tests/README.md`
+for `compare-bindings.py`, `compare-binding-closure.py --regenerate-support`,
+and `verify-kotlin-package.py` commands, including full trimming/R8 and NativeAOT.
+These probes are not substitutes for the host tests.
+
+`tests/BindingProjection/Corpus/README.md` documents whole-corpus generation and
+grouped-implementation JNI checks. Run `verify-smoke.py` against an actual grouped
+reference set and its native inputs with `--configuration Debug`, `Release`, and
+`NativeAOT`; every mode requires all 26 checks, not just successful installation.
+
+The customer-shaped binding projection solution is
+`tests/BindingProjection/Reference.slnx`. Build it normally with
+`./dotnet-local.sh build tests/BindingProjection/Reference.slnx -c Debug -nr:false`.
+Its README documents the locked native graph, separate Reader/Writer libraries,
+minimal contracts, ownership validation, and verification-only device runner.
+Use `--filter 'FullyQualifiedName~BindingViewProjection|FullyQualifiedName~IndirectInterfaceMappings'`
+in generator tests and `--filter 'FullyQualifiedName~ExperimentalBindingsTests'`
+in `Xamarin.Android.Build.Tests.dll` for focused host regressions.
+
+`tests/BindingProjection/GeneratorPackage/README.md` documents the separate
+stock-workload package integration fixture. It restores the local compiler
+NuGet without fork-only imports and covers no-op generation, no-clean
+Legacy/Semantic switching, metadata, missing generated files, multi-targeting,
+design-time compilation, strict MT tasks, runtime dependency flow and package
+upgrades. Its explicit-device option runs 11 actual JNI checks in each of Debug,
+Release/full-trim/R8, and NativeAOT, including managed callbacks and generic views.
+
+`tests/BindingProjection/MauiCompatibility/README.md` documents the separate
+real-MAUI protected-binding pilot. `verify-pilot.py` extracts full/usage-selected
+contracts from shipped MAUI DLLs, freezes an old consumer, regenerates
+SwipeRefreshLayout under its original owner, verifies the compiled contract,
+and optionally runs 13 checks each in Debug, full-trim/R8 and NativeAOT.
+Identity-only exposure does not automatically pin every legacy overload;
+subclass/implementation and implicit legacy interop uses are recorded separately.
+
